summary: core/io's line reader lends each line of core/io.memory's standard input without its ending, reading \r\n as \n and keeping a lone \r, gives empty lines and an unterminated last line, reports a line longer than its buffer as line_too_long and gives the line after it next, reads the same lines when every read is three bytes and a \r\n is split between reads, and keeps what it read across an injected read failure; the end of input is a finished line, every time it is asked again
